<title>USA: Coventry Corp unit sells medical offices.</title>
<headline>Coventry Corp unit sells medical offices.</headline>
<dateline>NASHVILLE, Tenn. 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coventry Corp said on Friday that its HealthAmerica subsidiary in Pittsburgh has agreed in principle to sell its medical practices to Allegheny Health, Education and Research Foundation for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>Included in the sale would be Penn Group Medical Associates, with nine offices in the Pittsburgh area.</p>
<p>The physicians in the practices being sold will continue to treat HealthAmerica members under a 10-year alliance with Allegheny that would be part of the deal.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
